# Build context for the root-context images: Core, Analysis and the docs site.
#
# Without this file every one of those builds uploaded the whole repository to the
# daemon -- including `node_modules/` (hundreds of MB), every service's `.venv/`,
# the Playwright artefacts and the local `.env`. That is slow, it invalidates the
# cache on any unrelated file change, and a local `.env` inside a build context is
# one careless `COPY . .` away from being baked into a published image.
#
# Deliberately a denylist rather than an allowlist: the three Dockerfiles that use
# this context copy explicit paths, so anything missed here costs upload time, not
# correctness.

# Version control and CI
.git
.gitignore
.github
.agents
.claude
.codex
.superpowers

# Python environments and caches
**/.venv
**/venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/*.egg-info

# Node
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/.pnpm-store

# Local configuration and secrets. `.env.example` is the committed template and is
# intentionally not excluded.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Test and build output
**/test-results
**/playwright-report
**/blob-report
site/
specs/out/
logs/

# Editor and OS noise
.idea
.vscode
**/.DS_Store
**/*.swp
